<article class="env-remark" id="0371">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0371">Remark <span data-tag="0371">95.15.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $G$ be an abstract group. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $G \to \text{Aut}_ S(X)$ be a group homomorphism. In this setting we can define $[[X/G]]$ similarly to the above as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
An object of $[[X/G]]$ consists of a triple $(U, P, \varphi : P \to X)$ where 
</p>
<ol>
  <li><p>
$U$ is an object of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$P$ is a sheaf on $(\mathit{Sch}/U)_{fppf}$ which comes with an action of $G$ that turns it into a torsor under the constant sheaf with value $G$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\varphi : P \to X$ is a $G$-equivariant map of sheaves. 
</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li><li><p>
A morphism $(f, g) : (U, P, \varphi ) \to (U', P', \varphi ')$ is given by a morphism of schemes $f : T \to T'$ and a $G$-equivariant isomorphism $g : P \to f^{-1}P'$ such that $\varphi = \varphi ' \circ g$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In exactly the same manner as above we obtain a functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [[X/G]] \longrightarrow (\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}  \]
</div>
  <p> which turns $[[X/G]]$ into a stack in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. The constant sheaf $\underline{G}$ is (provided the cardinality of $G$ is not too large) representable by $G_ S$ on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ and this version of $[[X/G]]$ is equivalent to the stack $[[X/G_ S]]$ introduced above. </p>
</article>